WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.593
Here's the frame for the whole guide:

2
00:00:02.593 --> 00:00:06.275
Book 08's design, mapped
onto the way Infoblox works.

3
00:00:06.275 --> 00:00:11.369
Book 08 wants governed DNS and address
management, and on NIOS that's a Grid,

4
00:00:11.369 --> 00:00:14.626
one Grid Master holding
the database and every

5
00:00:14.626 --> 00:00:18.050
member getting its copy
over an encrypted tunnel.

6
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:23.169
Book 08 wants a period of coexistence
with Microsoft, so NIOS first manages

7
00:00:23.169 --> 00:00:28.288
the Windows servers read-only, then takes
over zones and scopes one at a time.

8
00:00:28.288 --> 00:00:33.713
Book 08 requires DNSSEC, so the Grid
Master signs as a hidden primary.

9
00:00:33.713 --> 00:00:38.949
And its evidence becomes syslog, audit
logs, backups and the STIG checklist.

10
00:00:38.949 --> 00:00:44.900
Book 08's six phases still govern, but
this guide adds a Phase 0 of decisions.
